---
scope: "The document-structure contract that makes a .lts document able to ADDRESS ITSELF and to ASSERT what it contains. Four parts: (1) the REQUIRED document root form — frontmatter including `audience` and `elements`, and the document id declared IN THE H1 — made a linted contract so file 73 cannot repeat the lapse, plus the repair of the five files that fail it; (2) `elements` as MANDATORY frontmatter declaring the document's own element namespace, narrowest-covering, expressing AUTHORED INTENT rather than current output, and checked by the linter without ever becoming the containment mechanism; (3) the INFLATION CHECK — a bracket whose text matches a declared element prefix but which produced NO NODE is a reported failure, scoped to structural positions on a measured census, plus the three converse checks; (4) the bracketed-key silent-loss class, and the general rule that a control which does not exercise a shape found in live corpora certifies a narrower class than its name claims."
audience: [factlattice-maintainer, the builder implementing the linter rules and the five-file repair, composeux-architect (ratifies before dispatch; no decision point in this document is open any longer), David (ruled the root form, the mandatory element declaration and the bracketed-key verdict, all 2026-08-11), anyone who later asks why the parser was NOT taught a second document-root spelling, why `elements` may not be derived from what a file already mints, or why `- [ID]: description` is flagged rather than minted as an untyped edge]
elements: [DRI-*, DD-DRI-*]
boundary: "IN: the REQUIRED document root form and its lint finding ([DRI-ROOT-REQUIRED]); the h1 id form per document tag, including the two non-SPEC documents ([DRI-ROOT-BY-DOCTYPE]); the repair of the five non-conformant files and the recorded rejection of the parser-side alternative ([DRI-REPAIR]); the no-migration compatibility requirement ([DRI-NO-MIGRATION]); the MANDATORY `elements` declaration, its narrowness rule and the intent-not-output rule that makes it an instrument rather than a mirror ([DRI-ELEMENTS-DECL], [DRI-ELEMENTS-NARROW], [DRI-ELEMENTS-INTENT]); the inflation check, its normalization rule, its measured scope and the three converse checks ([DRI-INFLATION], [DRI-INFLATION-MATCH], [DRI-INFLATION-SCOPE], [DRI-CONVERSE]); the bracketed-key silent-loss class and the control cases that must exercise it in the LIVE shape ([DRI-BRACKET-KEY], [DRI-CONTROL-CASES]); the general control-narrowness rule ([DRI-CONTROL-SHAPE]); why element ids must NOT be re-namespaced ([DRI-ID-GRAMMAR]); the error matrix and the two-tier acceptance bar. OUT: any parser change to document-root recognition (RULED OUT by David 2026-08-11, recorded with its evidence at [DRI-REPAIR]); any change to the 67 conforming files BEYOND adding the newly-required `elements` key; any migration of existing element ids (explicitly FORBIDDEN, [DRI-ID-GRAMMAR]); the six other open silent-loss classes; the SL register's numbering authority, which is read at merge time, not restated."
not-this: "Not a second document-root spelling. David ruled 2026-08-11 that teaching the parser a bare-line root would install the two-conventions problem this corpus spent the day removing — P2 Notation Freedom was for ENCODING flexibility, not for two spellings of one construct. Not a new containment mechanism: containment stays STRUCTURALLY DERIVED from heading nesting, and the `elements` declaration is a checksum over it, never a second source of truth. Not an OPT-IN declaration — as an opt-in the inflation check fires zero times until somebody volunteers, and a rule that reports zero looks exactly like a rule that works ([DRI-ELEMENTS-DECL]). Not a declaration DERIVED from the nodes a file currently mints — that would be a control fitted to its own result, and it is the single most likely wrong implementation ([DRI-ELEMENTS-INTENT]). Not a re-namespacing of element ids: the colon is already the doctype separator, so [CXC-IH:5A] parses as doctype CXC-IH plus id 5A, and 5A fails the id grammar — proposing it would MANUFACTURE the exact silent loss this spec exists to end. Not an untyped edge: David ruled 2026-08-11 that `- [ID]: description` is FLAGGED with a finding carrying its repair and mints NOTHING — minting an untyped edge would install an edge state the model does not have, which is a MODEL change riding in on a parser convenience, and it would resolve this ambiguous-key case in the opposite direction to the same day's ruling on parenthetical qualifier drops ([DD-DRI-BRACKET-KEY-VERDICT]). Every decision point in this document is now CLOSED."
