## 7. Error and boundary matrix

### [DRI-BOUNDARIES] Every condition a builder would otherwise have to invent an answer for

| # | Condition | Required behaviour |
|---|-----------|--------------------|
| 1 | conforming file — frontmatter with `audience`, id in the h1 | clean; no rule in this spec touches it ([DRI-NO-MIGRATION]) |
| 2 | no frontmatter block at all | ERROR naming the rule and the exemplar (spec 29) |
| 3 | frontmatter present, `audience` absent | ERROR naming the rule and the exemplar |
| 4 | h1 carries no bracketed id | ERROR; the finding also names any column-0 bracketed line in the first 10 lines as the probable intended root |
| 5 | column-0 `[TAG:ID]` line after a bracketless h1 | NEVER parsed as a root; it is a diagnostic hint inside finding 4 ([DRI-REPAIR]) |
| 6 | h1 id fails the id grammar (lowercase, punctuation, leading digit) | treated as a bracketless h1, with the failed condition named; never normalized |
| 7 | h1 id carries no doctype (`# Title [ID]`) | finding — invisible to `find(doctype=…)` ([DRI-ROOT-BY-DOCTYPE]) |
| 8 | h1 id carries a tag no profile or core registers | ERROR; a repair MUST NOT invent a tag |
| 9 | two `h1` lines, or a second bracketed h1 id | ERROR naming both lines; no precedence resolution |
| 10 | non-SPEC document (`LEDGER`, `REGISTRY`, `PROFILE`, `SYSTEM`, `PROJECT`) | same rule, same severity; the tag table at [DRI-ROOT-BY-DOCTYPE] is exhaustive |
| 11 | repair would require renaming a node id | FORBIDDEN — preserve the id, change only its position ([DRI-NO-MIGRATION]) |
| 12 | no `elements` key in frontmatter | ERROR — mandatory; 72 of 72 files on day one ([DRI-ELEMENTS-DECL]) |
| 12a | `elements` declared as a prefix broader than the document's family (`CXC-*`) | ERROR naming the narrowest covering pattern ([DRI-ELEMENTS-NARROW]) |
| 12b | the same pattern declared by more than one document | finding naming every declaring document — a namespace nobody owns is not a namespace |
| 12c | two declared patterns in one document, one a strict prefix of the other | ERROR — the broader makes the narrower dead text |
| 12d | more than three patterns needed to cover one document | reported as over-fragmented; declaration stands, checks still run; 4 live files ([DRI-ELEMENTS-NARROW]) |
| 12e | a declaration DERIVED from the nodes the file currently mints | UNVALIDATED, never clean — a control fitted to its own result ([DRI-ELEMENTS-INTENT]) |
| 12f | an authored id that never minted, under a declared pattern | the declaration MUST still cover it, so inflation FAILS — that failure is the instrument working |
| 13 | `elements` pattern with a mid-pattern wildcard | ERROR at lint time; trailing glob only |
| 14 | `elements` declared, bracket matches, node exists in THIS file | clean |
| 15 | `elements` declared, bracket matches, node exists in ANOTHER file | not inflation — a reference; evaluate for NAMESPACE LEAK instead |
| 16 | `elements` declared, bracket matches, node exists NOWHERE, STRUCTURAL position | INFLATION FAILURE (error), naming raw + normalized form |
| 17 | the same in a PROSE position | NO finding — 215 legitimate live cases ([DRI-INFLATION-SCOPE]) |
| 18 | bracket normalizes to empty (pure punctuation) | discard as non-candidate; never compare |
| 19 | node minted in this file matching no declared pattern | MISFILED (error) — root id exempt |
| 20 | declared pattern with zero minted nodes | DEAD DECLARATION (warning) |
| 21 | node under this file's pattern living in a file that does not declare it | NAMESPACE LEAK (warning), naming both files |
| 22 | two files declaring the SAME pattern, both minting under it | SHARED-FAMILY warning naming both; not a leak |
| 23 | leak check requested from a single-file lint | report NOT RUN; never report it as passing |
| 24 | `- [ID]: description` in a node body | FLAG with a finding naming the line and carrying both repairs; mint NO edge — DECIDED 2026-08-11 ([DD-DRI-BRACKET-KEY-VERDICT]); never both-nothing, never an invented edge type |
| 25 | any proposal to re-namespace element ids as `[FAMILY:ELEMENT]` | REFUSE — parses as doctype + invalid id and mints nothing ([DRI-ID-GRAMMAR]) |

- part-of: [SPEC:LTS-DOC-ROOT]

