## 8. Acceptance — two tiers, machine and glass

### [DRI-ACCEPT] Every requirement has a machine signal; every author-facing surface has a glass gate

- rule: a machine signal certifies the parse and the finding. Anything whose value is an AUTHOR reading a
  message also needs a glass gate, because a finding that is technically emitted and practically
  unreadable is the failure mode this whole class of work exists to end.

| ID | Requirement | `verify.machine` | `verify.human` (glass) |
|----|-------------|------------------|------------------------|
| DRI-C1 | **The required-form rule catches EXACTLY the 9 known violators on its first run** ([DRI-ROOT-REQUIRED]) | `tests/test_document_root_form.py::test_first_run_names_exactly_nine` — assert the finding set is exactly the 5 no-frontmatter files plus the 4 missing `audience`; no more, no fewer | — |
| DRI-C1B | **The `elements` rule reports EXACTLY 72 on its first run** ([DRI-ELEMENTS-DECL]) | `::test_elements_baseline_is_all_seventy_two` — assert every `.lts` in the corpus is named, including the exemplar; any other number means the rule is not reading every file | — |
| DRI-C1C | **A DERIVED declaration is caught, not trusted** ([DRI-ELEMENTS-INTENT]) | `tests/test_element_declaration.py::test_derived_declaration_misses_authored_id` — build a declaration from a file's minted nodes only; assert it does NOT cover that file's known non-minting authored id | — |
| DRI-C1D | Narrowest-covering is enforced ([DRI-ELEMENTS-NARROW]) | `::test_overbroad_pattern_refused` (a `PFX-*` over `PFX-SUB-*` elements errors and the message names the narrowest), `::test_shared_pattern_reported`, `::test_prefix_of_sibling_refused`, `::test_over_three_patterns_reported` — and a corpus run asserting exactly 4 files are over-fragmented | — |
| DRI-C2 | Every finding names the rule AND the exemplar | `::test_finding_names_rule_and_exemplar` — assert `29-composeux-embedded-reactive.lts` appears in every message | an author shown one finding can fix the file without opening a spec |
| DRI-C3 | The rule covers non-SPEC tags ([DRI-ROOT-BY-DOCTYPE]) | `::test_all_registered_tags_accepted` — `LEDGER`, `REGISTRY`, `PROFILE`, `SYSTEM`, `PROJECT` h1 forms are clean; an unregistered tag errors | — |
| DRI-C4 | A bracketless h1 names the probable intended root | `::test_bare_line_named_as_hint_not_parsed` — assert the column-0 bracketed line appears in the message AND that no node was minted from it | — |
| DRI-C5 | The five repairs mint their roots ([DRI-REPAIR]) | `::test_repaired_files_mint_roots` — after repair, each of the five declared ids resolves to a node with the expected `document_tag`, carries the document's own properties, and CONTAINS every deeper heading | in the console spec browser, opening one of the five lists its elements instead of an empty pane |
| DRI-C6 | **Zero change to the 67 conforming files** ([DRI-NO-MIGRATION]) | `::test_conforming_files_unchanged` — full-corpus parse before/after; assert the node set, property maps and edge set for those 67 files are identical, and that exactly 5 roots plus their structural edges appeared | — |
| DRI-C7 | No node id was renamed by the repair | `::test_no_id_renamed` — the corpus id set after repair is a strict superset of the id set before, with exactly 5 additions | — |
| DRI-C8 | `elements` changes NO edge ([DRI-ELEMENTS-DECL]) | `tests/test_element_declaration.py::test_declaration_is_inert_on_graph` — parse a file with and without the declaration; assert the edge set and `parent_section` values are byte-identical | — |
| DRI-C9 | Inflation normalization ([DRI-INFLATION-MATCH]) | `tests/test_inflation.py::test_normalization_table` — table-driven over the six rows of the worked table, positives AND negatives | — |
| DRI-C10 | **Prose brackets are NOT scanned** ([DRI-INFLATION-SCOPE]) | `::test_prose_position_not_scanned` — a matching, unresolvable bracket in prose, in a table cell and in a property value each yield NO finding; plus a corpus run asserting the total is far below the 215 a whole-file scan would emit | David or the architect reads the full finding list and judges every entry actionable |
| DRI-C11 | Inflation resolution is CORPUS-scoped ([DRI-INFLATION]) | `::test_cross_file_reference_is_not_inflation` — a bracket resolving to a node in another file yields no inflation finding | — |
| DRI-C12 | Inflation catches the mis-punctuated live case | `::test_mispunctuated_id_flagged` — `[CXC-IH:5A]` under `elements: CXC-IH-*` in a structural position yields a finding naming both forms | the finding text names the raw form, the normalized form, and the declared prefix it matched |
| DRI-C13 | The three converses ([DRI-CONVERSE]) | `::test_misfiled`, `::test_dead_declaration`, `::test_namespace_leak` — one finding each at the specified severity | — |
| DRI-C14 | Leak check reports NOT RUN in single-file mode | `::test_leak_not_run_is_not_pass` — assert the result is distinguishable from a pass | — |
| DRI-C15 | Bracketed key is FLAGGED and mints nothing ([DRI-BRACKET-KEY], [DD-DRI-BRACKET-KEY-VERDICT]) | `tests/test_bracket_key.py::test_bracket_key_is_flagged_and_mints_no_edge` — assert exactly one finding names the line, assert the edge count is UNCHANGED by the line, and assert the message contains both repair forms; the disjunction is gone because the verdict was ruled 2026-08-11 | an author shown the finding re-authors the line correctly without opening this spec |
| DRI-C16 | The control exercises the LIVE shapes ([DRI-CONTROL-CASES]) | `tests/test_selfcheck_shape_coverage.py::test_control_contains_live_shapes` — assert the control file literally contains each shape in the [DRI-CONTROL-CASES] table, including the prose sub-case of the non-candidate row | a reviewer can answer "which live shapes does this control contain" by reading the control |

- requirement: DRI-C1, DRI-C1B, DRI-C1C, DRI-C6 and DRI-C10 are the gates. DRI-C1 and DRI-C1B are the
  positive controls with exact counts — 9 and 72 — and a rule that finds a different number has either
  missed a known violator or invented one. **DRI-C1C is the gate that protects every other measurement in
  this spec**: a build that passes it cannot have fitted the declaration to its own result, and a build
  that fails it has produced a corpus of declarations under which the inflation check can never find
  anything. A build failing DRI-C6 has broken 67 working documents to fix 5. A build failing DRI-C10 has
  shipped a check that will be switched off.
- part-of: [SPEC:LTS-DOC-ROOT]

