**Version**: 0.4
**Created**: 2026-08-11
**Status**: Draft — ALL DECISION POINTS CLOSED. Revised 2026-08-11 after David's THIRD ruling:
**[DD-DRI-BRACKET-KEY-VERDICT] is CLOSED — FLAG, do not mint.** `- [ID]: description` produces a NAMED
FINDING carrying its own repair (write `- [ID] **Title**` for a NODE, or a `## Relationships` triple for
a TYPED edge) and mints NO edge. The edge TYPE is not in the syntax — it is in the section title — so
minting means inventing a semantic the author never wrote, and an invented edge is a SUBSTITUTION, which
this corpus has established is strictly worse than a LOSS: a missing edge is detectable by the very
checks in this spec, a plausible wrong one is not (SL-18, where `zb.ds.GOVERNS` silently became
`GOVERNS`; and the widened matcher that already fabricated an edge to `-55]`). The decisive evidence is
CONSISTENCY: David ruled identically hours earlier the same day on the parenthetical qualifier drops
(`- key (qualifier): value`, 28 live in specs 58 and 59 alone), for the same reason and with the same
repair shape, and resolving two ambiguous-key situations in opposite directions would make the format
incoherent with itself. The rejected branch — mint an explicitly UNTYPED edge, which would have
recovered [CXC-IH-EDGES]' three real lost edges and generalised — is KEPT at full strength in the node
with its `invalidating_assumption`: the objection is to inventing the untyped-edge STATE here as a
parser convenience, not to the state existing, so a first-class ratified untyped edge reopens this on its
merits. Revised 2026-08-11 after David's second ruling: **`elements` is a
HARD REQUIREMENT in frontmatter on every document**, not an optional declaration — as an opt-in the
inflation check fires zero times until somebody volunteers, and a rule that reports zero looks exactly
like a rule that works ([DRI-ELEMENTS-DECL]). Two clauses make the mechanism non-decorative and both are
in the spec text: the pattern must be the NARROWEST that covers, and a pattern shared across documents is
itself a finding ([DRI-ELEMENTS-NARROW], measured — `CXC-*` covers 100% of spec 29 and is worthless;
`CXC-ER-*` is the useful declaration; 67 of 71 files are coverable by at most three patterns, and the
four that are not must be named); and the declaration expresses AUTHORED INTENT, never current output
([DRI-ELEMENTS-INTENT]) — a declaration derived from a file's minted nodes is a control fitted to its own
result, would let every existing file pass by construction, and is the same failure D3 documents one
layer down. Baseline for the new key: **0 of 72 files declare `elements` today, including the exemplar**,
so the first run reports 72. Also revised 2026-08-11 after David's first ruling: the parser is NOT taught
a bare-line document root; the five non-conformant files are REPAIRED to the exemplar
(`29-composeux-embedded-reactive.lts`) and the document root form becomes a REQUIRED, LINTED contract.
The rejection is recorded with its evidence and its `invalidating_assumption` at [DRI-REPAIR], not
silently deleted. Two decision points DISSOLVED with R1 (`DD-DRI-ROOT-TITLE`, `DD-DRI-UNTAGGED-ROOT` —
with the id in the h1 there is one title rule and one existing form; the untagged-id question survives as
the note at [DRI-ROOT-BY-DOCTYPE]). One decision point was SETTLED by census and is now a plain node:
[DRI-INFLATION-SCOPE], structural-positions-only, decided by 215 measured false positives a whole-file
scan would emit. NO decision point remains open. What still gates dispatch is not a fork but a normal
ratify of the whole document, plus the register number: the silent-loss class named at [DRI-BRACKET-KEY]
takes its number
at merge time from `docs/improvement_suggestions/coordination/silent-loss-classes.md` (highest assigned
at v5: SL-18); this document deliberately reserves none. Node ids are NOT migrated and MUST NOT be
([DRI-ID-GRAMMAR]).
**Intelligence**: composed by `factlattice-editor` from the composeux-architect's narrative brief and
revised against David's 2026-08-11 ruling; grounded against `factlattice/parser.py`,
`factlattice/coverage.py`, `factlattice/selfcheck/control.lts`, the `.lts` domain profile
`corpora/intelligence-console/platform-composeio-profile.lts`, the exemplar
`29-composeux-embedded-reactive.lts`, the five non-conformant documents, and the silent-loss register.
